{
  "id": 461993410,
  "iid": 23814,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Add DATA_INDICATION check for MS-TURN packets",
  "description": "MS-TURN uses the STUN message type `0x0115` for `DataIndication`, which does not align with the standard defined in RFC5389. Currently, MS-TURN messages with header type `0x0115` are interpreted as an \"Unknown Error Response\". This patch fixes that.\n\nBefore `col_add_lstr`, checks were added to verify whether `MAGIC_COOKIE` is the first attribute, as this is the criterion used to distinguish MS-TURN packets. If this condition is met and the `msg_type` is `0x0115`, the message is interpreted as `DATA_INDICATION`.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-03-08T14:26:07.333Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-09T06:52:27.305Z",
